The 1934–35 Scottish football season was [[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]]'s 47th season of competitive football, in which they competed in the [[Scottish First Division]]<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.londonhearts.com/scores/a1930/celtic1935.htm|title=Results for Celtic for 1934-35|website=www.londonhearts.com}}</ref> and the [[Scottish Cup]].

Celtic notoriously narrowed the previous year's gap with defending champions [[Rangers F.C.|Rangers]], but in the end finished runners-up to the [[Govan]] club, 52 points to their neighbours' 55.

In the Scottish Cup, Celtic were eliminated by [[Aberdeen F.C.|Aberdeen]] 3-1 away in the fourth round (quarter-finals).

